        "original_id": "63ae7dfe-f6a5-57c8-a589-1a6804fb9801",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Danny Bonaduce, Joseph Bonaduce, Bonnie Franklin, Mackenzie Phillips, Valerie Bertinelli\n- TV Shows: One Day at a Time, I Know My Kid's a Star, The Partridge Family, The Dick Van Dyke Show\n- Places: Broomall, Pennsylvania, Indianapolis\n- Roles: radio/television personality, comedian, professional wrestler, child actor, TV writer, producer, host, judge\n\nFacts:\n- Danny Bonaduce was born on August 13, 1959.\n- Danny Bonaduce was born in Broomall, Pennsylvania.\n- Danny Bonaduce is an American radio/television personality, comedian, professional wrestler, and former child actor.\n- Joseph Bonaduce is Danny Bonaduce's father and was a veteran TV writer and producer.\n- Joseph Bonaduce worked on The Dick Van Dyke Show and One Day at a Time.\n- One Day at a Time was an American sitcom that aired on CBS from December 16, 1975, to May 28, 1984.\n- One Day at a Time starred Bonnie Franklin as a divorced mother raising two teenage daughters in Indianapolis.\n- Mackenzie Phillips and Valerie Bertinelli played the two teenage daughters on One Day at a Time.\n- Danny Bonaduce was known as a child actor on the 1970s TV show The Partridge Family.\n- Danny Bonaduce was the host and primary judge of I Know My Kid's a Star.",
